    {
      "extracted_at": "2026-06-18T21:05:04Z",
      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "On March 2, 2021, the district court granted NVIDIA's motion to dismiss the complaint without leave to amend, entered judgment in favor of NVIDIA and closed the case. On March 30, 2021, plaintiffs filed an appeal from judgment in the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, case number 21-15604. Oral argument is scheduled for May 10, 2022.",
            "entity_name": "In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative lawsuit pending in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California, captioned 4:19-cv-00341-HSG, initially filed January 18, 2019 and titled In re NVIDIA Corporation Consolidated Derivative Litigation, was stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action. On February 22, 2022, the court administratively closed the case, but stated that it would reopen the case once the appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action is resolved.",
            "entity_name": "In re NVIDIA Corporation Consolidated Derivative Litigation",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative actions initially filed September 24, 2019 and pending in the United States District Court for the District of Delaware, Lipchitz v. Huang, et al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01795-UNA) and Nelson v. Huang, et. al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01798- UNA), remain stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action.",
            "entity_name": "Lipchitz v. Huang, et al.",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative actions initially filed September 24, 2019 and pending in the United States District Court for the District of Delaware, Lipchitz v. Huang, et al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01795-UNA) and Nelson v. Huang, et. al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01798- UNA), remain stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action.",
            "entity_name": "Nelson v. Huang, et al.",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "As of January 30, 2022, we have a remaining authorization, subject to certain specifications, to repurchase shares of our common stock up to $7.24 billion through December 2022. From January 31, 2022 through March 17, 2022, we repurchased 7.7 million shares of our common stock for $1.75 billion.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA FY2022 Share Repurchase Remaining Authorization",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "During fiscal years 2022, 2021, and 2020, we paid $399 million, $395 million, and $390 million in cash dividends to our shareholders, respectively.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA FY2022 Cash Dividends",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "In June 2021, March 2020, and September 2016, we issued a total of $5.00 billion, $5.00 billion, and $2.00 billion aggregate principal of senior notes, respectively. The net proceeds from these offerings were $4.98 billion, $4.97 billion, and $1.98 billion, respectively, after deducting debt discount and issuance costs.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA June 2021 $5.0B Senior Notes Issuance",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "On August 16, 2021, we repaid the $1.00 billion of 2.20% Notes Due 2021.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA August 2021 Repayment of 2.20% Notes Due 2021",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Our Graphics segment includes GeForce GPUs for gaming and PCs, the GeForce NOW game streaming service and related infrastructure, and solutions for gaming platforms; Quadro/NVIDIA RTX GPUs for enterprise workstation graphics; vGPU software for cloud-based visual and virtual computing; automotive platforms for infotainment systems; and Omniverse software for building 3D designs and virtual worlds.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Graphics Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Our Compute & Networking segment includes Data Center platforms and systems for AI, HPC, and accelerated computing; Mellanox networking and interconnect solutions; automotive AI Cockpit, autonomous driving development agreements, and autonomous vehicle solutions; CMP; Jetson for robotics and other embedded platforms; and NVIDIA AI Enterprise and other software.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Compute & Networking Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Gaming$12,462 $7,759 $5,518",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Gaming End Market",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Data Center10,613 6,696 2,983",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Data Center End Market",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On June 28, 2021, we simplified our corporate structure by repatriating the economic rights of certain non-U.S. IP to the United States via domestication of a foreign subsidiary, or the Domestication. The Domestication more closely aligns our corporate structure to our operating structure in accordance with the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development's Base Erosion and Profit Shifting conclusions and changes to U.S. and European tax laws. The impact of the Domestication, which is regarded as a change in tax status, resulted in a discrete benefit primarily from re-valuing certain deferred tax assets, net of deferred tax liabilities, of $244 million in fiscal year 2022.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA IP Domestication FY2022",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
